  "worked_solution": "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\n$P(8,7)$ means the same thing as ${}_{8}{P}_{7}.$ Using the usual formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(8,7) & =\\frac{8!}{(8-7)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8!}{1!} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1}{1} \\\\  & =8\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =40\\,320.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
